# Environment keys the BigBase binary REQUIRES at startup in production.
#
# The deploy config-preflight (.github/workflows/deploy.yml, Phase 4.5) asserts
# each of these is present and non-empty in /opt/bigbase/.env BEFORE swapping the
# binary. A missing key fails the deploy job instead of bricking the service and
# forcing an auto-rollback — the recurrence guard for the Aug 12 incident where
# BIGBASE_ROOT_ENCRYPTION_KEY was never provisioned on the VPS.
#
# Format: one KEY name per line (no value). Blank lines and #comments ignored.
# Only list keys that HARD-FAIL startup — optional keys with defaults must NOT
# go here, or every deploy would false-fail.

BIGBASE_ROOT_ENCRYPTION_KEY
